# PART 10 — WORKSPACE OVERVIEW

## 13. Individual Confusion Workspace

Preserve the current visual design.

Display:

- Original confusion.
- Source.
- Current understanding status.
- Understanding date, if available.
- Four-stage learning progress.
- Quick Revisit access.

The four stages should remain independently clickable:

Capture → Clarify → Act → Reflect

Use checkmarks to indicate recorded learning activity.

Do not use checkmarks to represent mastery.

### Stage Completion Logic

Capture:
A valid confusion note exists.

Clarify:
At least one meaningful clarification response or knowledge-gap selection exists.

Act:
At least one meaningful help preference, question draft, or planned strategy has been recorded.

Reflect:
The student has recorded at least one actual strategy used and/or a meaningful evaluation or adaptation response.

Do not require every question within a stage to be answered.

Do not mark a stage complete simply because it was opened.

The four stages may all be complete while the student remains Still Confused.

### Understanding Status

Show a separate status badge:

- Still Confused.
- Partially Understood.
- Understood.

If no assessment exists, show a neutral "Not Checked Yet" placeholder.

Do not treat this placeholder as a fourth understanding outcome.

### Overview — Why This Matters

At the bottom of the workspace overview, add a small expandable section:

**Why This Matters ⓘ**

Collapsed by default.

Expanded text:

"Unstuck guides you from noticing confusion to identifying knowledge gaps, choosing learning strategies, evaluating what worked, and adjusting your next steps. You can move through the stages at your own pace."

Do not add academic citations yet.

