# PART 12 — DATA MODEL AND PERSISTENCE

## 15. Update localStorage Safely

Inspect the existing schema before changing it.

Preserve all existing records and saved text.

Extend the current data model to support:

- Clarification responses.
- Help preferences.
- Question drafts.
- Planned strategies.
- Strategy plan update timestamps.
- Actually used strategies.
- Helpful strategies.
- Approximate learning time.
- Adaptation decisions.
- Understanding status.
- Understanding history.
- Last meaningful activity.
- Stage completion evidence.

Suggested conceptual structure:

```javascript
{
  id,
  source,
  note,
  createdAt,
  updatedAt,

  clarify: {
    priorKnowledge,
    confusionCategories,
    confusionDetails
  },

  act: {
    helpPreference,
    questionDraft,
    plannedStrategies,
    planUpdatedAt
  },

  reflect: {
    actualStrategies,
    helpfulStrategies,
    timeSpent,
    nextDecision,
    updatedAt
  },

  understanding: {
    currentStatus,
    updatedAt,
    history: []
  }
}
```

Adapt this to the existing architecture rather than replacing the current schema blindly.

### Important Data Rules

- Planned strategies and actual strategies are separate.
- Helpful strategies must be a subset of actual strategies.
- Selecting a planned strategy does not imply it was used.
- Understanding status is independent of stage completion.
- All changes persist across browser refreshes.
- Old records must remain readable.
- Do not fabricate historical dates during migration.

If the existing application has old resolved/partially resolved statuses, migrate them conservatively without inventing missing information.

